/*!
\page page_stfsthitcollection StFstHitCollection — FST Hit Collection Documentation

\section fst_overview Overview

The Forward Silicon Tracker (FST) is a disk-based silicon-strip detector that reconstructs
charged-particle tracks at forward rapidities.  Reconstructed hits (1D strip clusters) are
organised in a four-level hierarchy of collection classes.  \ref StFstHitCollection is the
top-level object persisted in \c StEvent.  A companion class, \ref StFstEvtCollection,
stores the \e raw (pre-clustering) hit data from the same event.

\section fst_classes Classes in this group

| Class | Role |
|-------|------|
| \ref StFstHitCollection | Top-level event container for all FST reconstructed hits |
| \ref StFstWedgeHitCollection | Per-wedge container (one per wedge) |
| \ref StFstSensorHitCollection | Per-sensor container (one per sensor) |
| \ref StFstEvtCollection | Top-level event container for all FST \b raw hits |

\section fst_geometry Geometry constants (StFstConsts.h)

| Constant | Value | Meaning |
|----------|-------|---------|
| \c kFstNumDisk | 3 | Number of FST disks |
| \c kFstNumWedgePerDisk | 12 | Wedges per disk |
| \c kFstNumWedges | 36 | Total wedges (3 × 12) |
| \c kFstNumSensorsPerWedge | 3 | Sensors per wedge |
| \c kFstNumSensors | 108 | Total sensors (3 × 36) |

\section fst_hierarchy Containment hierarchy

\code{.unparsed}
StFstHitCollection                              (1 per event, in StEvent)
└── mWedges[kFstNumWedges = 36]                 (StFstWedgeHitCollection, stack-allocated)
    └── mSensors[kFstNumSensorsPerWedge = 3]    (StFstSensorHitCollection, stack-allocated)
        └── mHits                               (StSPtrVecFstHit — owns StFstHit objects)

StFstEvtCollection                              (1 per event, in StEvent, raw hits)
└── mRawHits                                    (StSPtrVecFstRawHit — owns StFstRawHit objects)
\endcode

\ref StFstHitCollection::addHit routes an incoming \ref StFstHit to the correct wedge
and sensor sub-collection using \c hit->getWedge()-1 (0-based wedge index) and
\c hit->getSensor() (0-based sensor index).

\section fst_ownership Object Ownership

\subsection fst_own_hit StFstHitCollection
\c mWedges[36] is a \b stack-allocated C-array of \ref StFstWedgeHitCollection objects —
no explicit destructor is required; they are destroyed with the parent.

\subsection fst_own_wedge StFstWedgeHitCollection
\c mSensors[3] is a \b stack-allocated C-array of \ref StFstSensorHitCollection objects —
same automatic lifetime as the parent.

\subsection fst_own_sensor StFstSensorHitCollection
\c mHits is a \c StSPtrVecFstHit (owning smart-pointer vector from \c StStrArray).
The destructor \b explicitly iterates over the vector and calls \c delete on each element.
This is required because \ref StFstHit provides a custom memory-pool \c operator
\c new / \c delete that is not compatible with the default \c StStrArray cleanup.
\warning Do not delete \ref StFstHit objects obtained from \ref StFstSensorHitCollection::hits.
The collection destructor owns them.

\subsection fst_own_evt StFstEvtCollection
\c mRawHits is a \c StSPtrVecFstRawHit (owning vector via \c StStrArray).
\c StStrArray automatically deletes the \ref StFstRawHit objects.  The
\ref StFstEvtCollection destructor is an explicit no-op.
\warning Do not delete \c StFstRawHit objects obtained from \ref StFstEvtCollection::rawHits.

\section fst_members Data Members

\subsection fst_mem_hit StFstHitCollection

| Type | Name | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| \c StFstWedgeHitCollection[36] | \c mWedges | Hit sub-collections, one per wedge (stack-allocated) |
| \c UChar_t | \c mClusteringType | Clustering algorithm type identifier |

\subsection fst_mem_wedge StFstWedgeHitCollection

| Type | Name | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| \c StFstSensorHitCollection[3] | \c mSensors | Hit sub-collections, one per sensor (stack-allocated) |

\subsection fst_mem_sensor StFstSensorHitCollection

| Type | Name | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| \c StSPtrVecFstHit | \c mHits | Owned vector of reconstructed hits on this sensor |

\subsection fst_mem_evt StFstEvtCollection

| Type | Name | Description |
|------|------|-------------|
| \c StSPtrVecFstRawHit | \c mRawHits | Owned vector of raw hits for the event |

\section fst_methods Key Methods

\subsection fst_meth_hit StFstHitCollection

| Signature | Description |
|-----------|-------------|
| \c bool addHit(StFstHit*) | Add a reconstructed hit; routes it to the correct wedge/sensor. Returns \c false if indices are out of range. |
| \c unsigned \c int \c numberOfHits() \c const | Total hits summed over all wedges and sensors |
| \c StFstWedgeHitCollection* \c wedge(unsigned \c int) | Wedge collection at 0-based index; \c nullptr if out of range |
| \c unsigned \c char \c getClusteringType() \c const | Clustering algorithm identifier |
| \c void \c setClusteringType(unsigned \c char) | Set clustering algorithm identifier |

\subsection fst_meth_wedge StFstWedgeHitCollection

| Signature | Description |
|-----------|-------------|
| \c unsigned \c int \c numberOfHits() \c const | Hits summed over all sensors in this wedge |
| \c StFstSensorHitCollection* \c sensor(unsigned \c int) | Sensor collection at 0-based index; \c nullptr if out of range |

\subsection fst_meth_sensor StFstSensorHitCollection

| Signature | Description |
|-----------|-------------|
| \c unsigned \c int \c numberOfHits() \c const | Number of hits on this sensor |
| \c StSPtrVecFstHit& \c hits() | Mutable reference to the hit vector |
| \c const \c StSPtrVecFstHit& \c hits() \c const | Read-only reference to the hit vector |

\subsection fst_meth_evt StFstEvtCollection

| Signature | Description |
|-----------|-------------|
| \c void \c addRawHit(StFstRawHit*) | Add a raw hit; validates channel ID and wedge index |
| \c unsigned \c int \c numberOfRawHits() \c const | Total raw hits in the event |
| \c StSPtrVecFstRawHit& \c rawHits() | Mutable reference to the raw-hit vector |
| \c void \c print(int) | Print a summary of the collection |

\section fst_example Usage Example

\code{.cpp}
// Iterate over reconstructed FST hits
const StFstHitCollection* fstColl = event->fstHitCollection();
if (!fstColl) return;

for (unsigned int iWedge = 0; iWedge < kFstNumWedges; ++iWedge) {
    const StFstWedgeHitCollection* wedge = fstColl->wedge(iWedge);
    if (!wedge) continue;

    for (unsigned int iSensor = 0; iSensor < kFstNumSensorsPerWedge; ++iSensor) {
        const StFstSensorHitCollection* sensor = wedge->sensor(iSensor);
        if (!sensor) continue;

        const StSPtrVecFstHit& hits = sensor->hits();
        for (const StFstHit* hit : hits) {
            // hit->position(), hit->getWedge(), hit->getSensor(), etc.
        }
    }
}

// Iterate over FST raw hits
const StFstEvtCollection* fstEvt = event->fstEvtCollection();
if (!fstEvt) return;

const StSPtrVecFstRawHit& rawHits = fstEvt->rawHits();
for (const StFstRawHit* rh : rawHits) {
    // rh->getWedge(), rh->getChannelId(), etc.
}
\endcode

*/
